  "text": "The longest river in the world is the Nile River.\n\nTo simplify the equation x/2 - 1/3 = 3x/4 + 5, we can eliminate the fractions by multiplying every term by the least common multiple of the denominators (2, 3, and 4), which is 12:\n\n12 * (x/2) - 12 * (1/3) = 12 * (3x/4) + 12 * 5\n\nThis simplifies to:\n6x - 4 = 9x + 60\n\nNext, we rearrange the terms to isolate x:\n6x - 9x = 60 + 4\n-3x = 64\n\nFinally, solve for x:\nx = -64/3"
